1.6.0

Build date: 2026-10-16

## Changelog

### 1.6.0 - 2026-10-16
- Added: 3 tracks (Small/Long/Longest), 8-checkpoint lap validation that
  catches teleport/respawn cheating, fences with deliberate gaps instead
  of no collision at all.
- Added: `.cgmap` custom track file format, save/export/open from the
  Maps folder, double-click-to-open file association.
- Added: admin mode (Settings > Car) gating a dev console (`/` to open,
  Minecraft-chat style), spectator free-fly camera (`/gamemode
  spectator`), NOS refill/unstick/minimap-teleport debug utilities.
- Added: standalone Map Editor (separate exe + Desktop shortcut) -- a
  top-down 2D tool for placing road control points and fence gaps,
  saving/opening the same `.cgmap` files the game reads, with a live
  preview of the real in-game road curve.
- Fixed: double-clicking a `.cgmap` file set the working directory to
  that file's folder instead of the exe's own, silently breaking every
  relative shader/asset load (ground/trees/cars rendering blank white).
- Fixed: the world's water plane showing through at any terrain dip
  below sea level, not just the intended lake.
- Fixed: fence rails stretching into stray near-vertical slivers on
  steep local terrain.
- Fixed: the dev console leaking keystrokes into gameplay hotkeys
  (e.g. typing "spectator" triggering pause).

### 1.5.0 - 2026-10-15
- Persistent per-car odometer: lifetime distance driven, saved to upgrades.cfg
  alongside the upgrade levels, shown in the Garage.

### 1.4.0 - 2026-10-15
- Fixed: AiTraffic and auto-drive both advanced along the road using a
  guessed, wrong sample spacing (2.2 units; the real circuit averages ~11.8),
  making every AI/auto-driven car move several times faster than its speed
  stat implied. Both now measure the real distance to the next sample.
- Fixed: drift tyre marks were drawn below the road surface mesh (at
  terrain height + 0.03 instead of the road's own + 0.14 lift), so they were
  never visible. Now share the road's real surface height.
- Added: best-lap ghost replay (Car::DrawGhost), traffic cars shown on the
  minimap, ambient wind sound layered into the engine audio.

### 1.3.0 - 2026-10-15
- Added: F toggles auto-drive, following the road directly (same approach
  as AiTraffic) rather than steering a physics body toward it.
- Added: visual drift slip (slipAngle_) and tyre-mark decals (SkidMarks).
- Reworked main menu: PLAY opens a Free Drive / Traffic Mode select screen;
  How To Play moved into Settings as its own tab.

### 1.2.0 - 2026-10-15
- Added: per-car upgrade system (Engine/Handling/Nitro, 0-3 levels each,
  persisted to upgrades.cfg), How To Play screen, 2 more cars (13 total).
- Fixed: Garage's BACK button was laid out past the bottom of the fixed
  720px canvas and was never visible, in windowed or fullscreen.

### 1.1.0 - 2026-10-15
- Added: Traffic Mode (AiTraffic -- AI cars looping the circuit).
- Fixed: fullscreen (F11) flashed black on every toggle (ToggleFullscreen()
  does a real display-mode switch). Switched to ToggleBorderlessWindowed()
  plus a fixed-resolution render target scaled/letterboxed into the real
  window, so the UI stays correctly laid out at any window size too.

### 1.0.0
- Baseline: original low-poly open-world driving game. Procedural car
  bodies and terrain, a full gearbox (auto/manual), NOS boost, drift
  scoring, lap timing, a 2-lap circuit, Kenney Nature Kit scenery, and a
  from-scratch engine-note synthesizer.
